.TH CLOG_CLOSE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
clog_close \- flush, close, and free a logger
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <clogger.h>

void clog_close(clog logger);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Releases all resources owned by the logger:
  - If the logger is file-backed and this is the last handle sharing
    the underlying file (i.e. all derived loggers have also been
    closed), the file descriptor is closed.  If derived loggers still
    exist the fd remains open and the file's ref-count is decremented.
  - All attached key=value fields are freed.
  - The internal write buffer is freed.
  - The per-handle state is freed; the shared backing store is freed
    only when the last handle is released.

After this call, the handle must not be used.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
logger  Logger handle to close.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
clog_close() must not be called while other threads are still calling
log_* macros on the same handle. Callers are responsible for ensuring
all logging threads have finished before calling clog_close().
For fd-based loggers (clog_open_fd_mp), the file descriptor is NOT
closed; it is the caller's responsibility.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR clog_open_fd_mp (3),
.BR clog_open_file_mp (3)
